# UI-WINDOW-1 fix round R4 (owner decision 2026-11-14, "Always show my city"; docs/re/ui.md 5.2):
# the status bar's materials and residents show on every screen while the local player owns a
# city. Over an island with one of the player's cities they show that city; anywhere else (open
# sea, an island without the player's city, the start camera) the player's first city in (island,
# city) order. `hud.counters` is what the last frame drew, `hud.counters.city` which city
# ("<island>:<city>", "none"). Fails on 919c59fc (R2's rule hid them away from the city island).
# Launch: --play data/maps/lan5.txt --construction-menu on --layout data/ui
resize 1024 768
wait frames 30
expect fact hud.counters == shown
expect fact hud.counters.city == 1:1
screenshot counters_start
lookw 700 700
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.counters == shown
expect fact hud.counters.city == 1:1
screenshot counters_sea
lookw 928 232
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.counters == shown
expect fact hud.counters.city == 1:1
look 1140 516
wait frames 5
expect fact hud.counters == shown
expect fact hud.counters.city == 1:1
screenshot counters_island
click_px 870 212
wait frames 3
expect fact ui.tab == player_list
expect fact hud.counters == shown
quit
